review_comment:
**issue (complexity):** Consider extracting WebSocket event handlers into dedicated methods to improve readability and reduce nesting complexity within the connect method, which will clarify responsibilities for WebSocket lifecycle, reconnection logic, and UI notifications while preserving functionality .

**Actionable Comment:**

Consider separating the reconnection logic and UI notifications from the low-level WebSocket event handling to reduce the nesting and improve readability. For example, extract event handlers into dedicated methods and consolidate reconnection attempts in one place:

```ts
private setupWebSocket(serverUrl: string): void {
    this.ws = new WebSocket(serverUrl);
    this.ws.addEventListener('open', this.handleOpen.bind(this));
    this.ws.addEventListener('error', this.handleError.bind(this));
    this.ws.addEventListener('close', () => this.handleClose(serverUrl));
}

private handleOpen(): void {
    this.reconnectAttempts = 0;
    vscode.window.showInformationMessage('Connected to collaboration server');
    // Resolve promise or notify connection success here
}

private handleError(): void {
    const error = new Error('WebSocket error occurred');
    vscode.window.showErrorMessage('WebSocket error: ' + error.message);
    // Reject promise or notify connection error here
}

private async handleClose(serverUrl: string): Promise<void> {
    vscode.window.showWarningMessage('Disconnected from collaboration server');
    if (this.shouldReconnect && this.reconnectAttempts < this.MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS) {
        this.reconnectAttempts++;
        vscode.window.showInformationMessage(`Attempting to reconnect (${this.reconnectAttempts}/${this.MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS})...`);
        try {
            // Attempt reconnection using the same setup method
            this.setupWebSocket(serverUrl);
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Reconnection failed:', error);
        }
    }
}

// Updated connect method delegating setup:
async connect(serverUrl: string): Promise<void> {
    this.shouldReconnect = true;
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        try {
            this.setupWebSocket(serverUrl);
            // Implement logic to resolve/reject promise after handling open/error events
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Connection error:', error);
            reject(error);
        }
    });
}
```

This refactoring clarifies each responsibility (WebSocket lifecycle, reconnection logic, and UI notifications) while preserving functionality.

