review_comment:
Empty `catch` blocks silently swallow errors, which can make debugging difficult. Consider logging caught errors in development mode (e.g., `console.warn(e)`) or at least documenting why they're safely ignored.
```suggestion
		} catch ( e ) {
			// Log the error in development mode for debugging purposes.
			// Safe to ignore as fallback logic ensures default values are used.
			if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
				console.warn('Error parsing navigation state from sessionStorage:', e);
			}
		}
```

