_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Error handling missing for module navigation.**

The `handleModuleSelect` function doesn't handle potential errors that might occur from the encoding process or during navigation.

Add a try/catch block to handle potential errors:

```diff
const handleModuleSelect = (moduleName: string) => {
  setOpen(false);
-  const encodedName = encodeModuleSlug(moduleName);
-  router.push(`/modules/${encodedName}`);
+  try {
+    const encodedName = encodeModuleSlug(moduleName);
+    router.push(`/modules/${encodedName}`);
+  } catch (error) {
+    console.error("Error navigating to module:", error);
+    // Provide user feedback about the navigation error
+  }
};
```


<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

`````suggestion
  const handleModuleSelect = (moduleName: string) => {
    setOpen(false);
    try {
      const encodedName = encodeModuleSlug(moduleName);
      router.push(`/modules/${encodedName}`);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Error navigating to module:", error);
      // Provide user feedback about the navigation error
    }
  };
`````

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

