DownloadsLabel backing field is initialized to an empty string, which can cause
it to show empty before the required Downloads property is set. To fix this,
initialize DownloadsLabel in the class constructor based on the initial value of
Downloads, or convert DownloadsLabel into a computed property that returns a
value derived from Downloads. If you choose the computed property approach,
ensure that OnPropertyChanged(nameof(DownloadsLabel)) is called within the
Downloads property's setter to notify UI updates.
