_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Consider refactoring static-only class to functions.**

The `Channel` class only contains static methods, which is flagged by the static analyzer. This pattern is generally discouraged in modern JavaScript/TypeScript.


Refactor the static-only class to exported functions:

```diff
-export class Channel {
-  static async find(id: string) {
+export async function findChannel(id: string) {
    return useDatabase().query.channels.findFirst({
      where: (channels, { eq }) => eq(channels.id, id),
    })
  }

-  static async create(data: ChannelDraft) {
+export async function createChannel(data: ChannelDraft) {
    const [channel] = await useDatabase()
      .insert(channels)
      .values(data)
      .returning()

    return channel
  }

-  static async update(id: string, data: Partial<ChannelDraft>) {
+export async function updateChannel(id: string, data: Partial<ChannelDraft>) {
    const [channel] = await useDatabase()
      .update(channels)
      .set(data)
      .where(eq(channels.id, id))
      .returning()

    return channel
  }

-  static async delete(id: string) {
+export async function deleteChannel(id: string) {
    await useDatabase().delete(channels).where(eq(channels.id, id))
  }
-}
```

This would require updating the Repository class to use these functions instead.


