review_comment:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Consider alternative approaches for Open Graph metadata**

While adding Open Graph tags via the `Head` component from `next/head` works for social sharing, there are a few potential issues:

1. In Next.js App Router, `next/head` is deprecated in favor of the Metadata API
2. Social media crawlers typically don't execute JavaScript, so showing these tags only when a dialog is open might not work for social sharing
3. Metadata should be set at the page level for optimal social media preview generation


Consider using Next.js 13+ Metadata API instead of the `Head` component, and place the metadata at the page level rather than conditionally in a dialog:

```tsx
// In your page.tsx file
import type { Metadata } from 'next'

export async function generateMetadata({ params }): Promise<Metadata> {
  // Fetch your itinerary data here
  const data = await fetchItinerary(params.id)

  return {
    openGraph: {
      title: data.title,
      description: data.description || 'Lihat itinerary ini!',
      images: [
        {
          url: data.coverImage || '/default-image.jpg',
          width: 1200,
          height: 630,
        },
      ],
    },
  }
}
```


Also applies to: 347-353

