_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Locale fall-back can silently break translations**

`getMessages()` loads messages for the _current request locale_ (set via `getLocale()` or `unstable_setRequestLocale`).  
Here you override the locale **after** the framework already derived it (`getLocale()`), but you don’t pass the chosen locale to `getMessages()`. If `wlData.defaultLocale` differs from what Next-Intl expects, the file system lookup will fail silently and return `{}`.

Consider passing the locale explicitly:

```diff
- messages = await getMessages();
+ messages = await getMessages({locale});
```




<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

`````suggestion
  try {
    const isLocalExist = await isLocaleSet();
    console.log('isLocalExist', isLocalExist);
    if (isLocalExist) {
      locale = await getLocale();
    } else {
      locale = wlData?.defaultLocale || 'en';
    }
    messages = await getMessages({locale});
`````

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

