_🧹 Nitpick (assertive)_

**Shadowing `node_id` hampers readability and can mislead debuggers.**

The structured binding inside the loop re-uses the name `node_id`, hiding the outer variable.  Renaming avoids accidental misuse and clarifies intent.

```diff
-    for (auto const [node_id, token_it] : new_partial_resolutions) {
+    for (auto const [child_node_id, token_it] : new_partial_resolutions) {
         auto [it, inserted] = partial_resolutions_to_update.try_emplace(
-                node_id,
+                child_node_id,
                 std::vector<ColumnDescriptorTokenIterator>{}
         );
-        it->second.emplace_back(token_it);
+        it->second.emplace_back(token_it);
     }
```



